From abf75b3f2ce7358a2944856c657bd2ea13be9567 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 17:14:57 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] fix(kanban): priority migrate tolerates the sync
 clamp (clamp-equivalent CAS, capped restore)

Run 2 of the operator priority migrate (op c314f72a, 2026-11-12 17:04Z) was
refused on the hub: apply and the guarded restore both said "priorities changed;
capture a new manifest". The manifest is captured from the raw Board snapshot
(old=59000) but the sync pull's `_local_fields` stores `bounded(priority)` on
every received upsert, including an equal-version re-send, with no event and no
outbox op. 17 hub-origin above-cap rows read 1000 locally while the Board kept
the raw value, so the CAS could never pass and a re-capture would see the same
raw value again.

Approach (b): apply and restore treat a stored PRIORITY_CAP as holding an
above-cap manifest original (`kanban_priority.at_value`). Any other drift still
refuses. A guarded restore without --allow-legacy-rollback writes
min(old, PRIORITY_CAP) instead of refusing, so it never raises a card above the
cap; the flag still restores the exact legacy value. Canonical verify-restore
accepts the capped value. Rows the clamp touched but apply never wrote are left
alone by restore (no raise).
